NOTE ON THE GPL COMPONENT

`tools/imsg-dump/` is NOT covered by this license. It is licensed under
GPL-3.0 and carries its own LICENSE file in that directory, because it links
the GPL-licensed `imessage-database` crate.

It is invoked strictly as a subprocess and is never linked into the Python
code in `src/`. That process boundary is deliberate: it is what keeps the
core MIT-licensed while allowing the GPL parser to do the typedstream work
that nothing else does correctly. If you change how it is invoked or vendor
it into the core, re-examine the licensing consequences.
